WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:07.620
SCP-682 found itself hurtling through an unstable
dimensional rift and into some fresh new hell.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:13.949
682 rose from the dirt and mulch beneath its
body and found itself on Level 23 of the Backrooms

00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:19.060
– which had the distinguishing characteristic
of being a spherical planetoid formed from

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.140
the interlocking of countless towering trees.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.949
It was commonly known as the Petrified Garden,
and it was the first of many Backroom’s

00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:31.199
levels that took the form of a globe rather
than an infinite maze.

00:00:31.199 --> 00:00:36.070
I know that it is hard to imagine a spherical
world because in our native reality the planet

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:41.760
Earth is a flat plane with ice walls on the
side - hahaha, just kidding - the flat earth

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.480
model is an inaccurate and roundly discredited
conception of cosmography without any empirical

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.250
evidence to support it.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:54.199
Could you imagine if we were peddling that
kind of conspiratorial fiction here in a youtube

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:55.199
video?

00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:59.180
Anyway, back to our regularly scheduled program
about an indestructible lizard traveling through

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.590
another dimension.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:05.910
Nearly all of the tree specimens present on
Level 23 had equivalent species that were

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.240
native to the Frontrooms - A.K.A.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.260
our reality.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:16.140
There were birch trees, cedars, redwoods,
white oaks, and many more common types intertwined

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.520
with trees that were either long extinct or
never before seen on earth.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.700
To 682, a tree was a tree, but then again,
the keter-class SCP wasn’t known for having

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.409
a deep and abiding respect for nature.

00:01:29.409 --> 00:01:34.880
Right now, what was flashing through its reptilian
head was a need to inflict violence.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:41.110
Preferably on the Old Wanderer that warped
SCP-682 to Level 23, but really any entity

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:45.689
that crossed its path was liable to get a
taste of the old maw and claw.

00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:50.460
Thankfully, the Backrooms had a habit of deploying
wave after wave of bizarre creatures from

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.060
who knows where.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:56.729
Not more than a couple of levels ago, 682
had been faced with a veritable army of these

00:01:56.729 --> 00:02:00.920
Backrooms entities and came out of the fight
victorious.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.420
By this point, the hard-to-destroy reptile
was well-acquainted with death rats, death

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:11.020
moths, clumps, smilers, and hounds – all
of which were no doubt lurking somewhere in

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.210
the woodwork of level 23.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:20.320
You can run, you can hide, but I will find
you and destroy you.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:25.050
SCP-682 was on the hunt once again, walking
through the entangled mess of trees like an

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.990
unstoppable engine of rage.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:33.581
It had certainly been some time since SCP-682
had encountered an entirely new entity, though

00:02:33.581 --> 00:02:37.300
it wasn’t exactly clamoring for a new lore
expansion.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:42.560
Since 682 was a being that despised all forms
of life and wanted to destroy it, the reptile

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.269
had the outlook of: the less entities that
were present throughout the Backrooms, the

00:02:47.269 --> 00:02:48.269
better.

00:02:48.269 --> 00:02:53.519
So when The Volpe appeared before SCP-682,
the anomalous monster was less than thrilled.

00:02:53.519 --> 00:02:57.930
But I’ll bet that you viewers at home are
excited to get to know a brand new Backrooms

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.230
entity after such a long wait.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.370
So why don’t we give you the Car Facts?

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.370
Um…

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:04.370
Car Fox?

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.370
Fox Facts?

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.890
We’re going to tell you about the Volpe
now, which no matter how it appears to the

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:12.430
untrained eye is not, in fact, a fox.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:18.269
The Volpe’s entity number is 119, and its
name comes from the Corsican word for “fox”

00:03:18.269 --> 00:03:23.209
– but I must once again clarify, this entity
is not actually a fox.

00:03:23.209 --> 00:03:28.220
The easiest ways to distinguish a volpe from
its more well-known counterpart in the frontrooms

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.819
are the abnormally elongated snout and the
secondary tail.

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:37.630
Volpes have been known to dwell almost exclusively
in levels of the Backrooms that display forest-like

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:39.010
characteristics.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:44.099
Which one could imagine would be very few
of them, but genuinely who knows at this point?

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:48.370
There could be an infinite number of infinite
forests infinitely scattered across infinite

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.400
layers of the Backrooms.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:54.540
And if that were to be the case, there would
be an infinite number of Volpes in all of

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.540
them.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:04:01.319
An entity 119 in its natural habitat will
dwell within a subterranean den, where the

00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:06.700
volpe digs itself in order to provide shelter
and protect itself from low temperatures.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.900
These dens can be unusually elaborate and
may comprise multiple branching tunnels and

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.989
security measures such as collections of twigs
that can alert the volpe to intruders when

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.269
they are disturbed.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:22.000
This complexity is somewhat warranted, because
the volpe stores a plentiful stash of food

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.570
deep within the den making it very unlikely
for them to go hungry.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.050
These volpes are rather clever, aren’t they?

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:35.740
Perhaps they are, but not quite clever enough
to avoid being effortlessly crushed by SCP-682

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:39.020
as it brought its two front claws down on
top of the entity.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.539
Better luck next time, entity 119.

00:04:41.539 --> 00:04:44.130
Not that there will be a next time.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:49.210
SCP-682 continued to move along the surface
of the planetoid and eventually entered into

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.310
a cavern created by the intertwining roots.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:57.530
Delving beneath Level 23’s forested crust,
the reptile found itself inside of a Glow

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:02.740
Room – a underground chamber lit by the
bioluminescence of glowworm-like entities

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:06.070
which had been given the name Gardener’s
Sorries.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.550
As their name would imply, these creatures
constantly made noises that sounded vaguely

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:12.759
like the word “sorry…”

00:05:12.759 --> 00:05:17.630
These pitiful worms crawled around the glowing
fungi and smaller flora making their signature

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:24.530
noises, and SCP-682 was absolutely not sorry
to messily devour every one of the Gardener’s

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:25.530
Sorries.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:29.990
The room was much darker with the absence
of the Gardener’s Sorries, but only temporarily

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:36.810
so: as SCP-682 was able to take on a bioluminescent
glow of its own and light its way deeper beneath

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:39.470
the surface of Level 23.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:44.700
It soon entered an area of ancient ruins that
seemed manmade yet overgrown with moss and

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.389
long abandoned.

00:05:46.389 --> 00:05:52.430
SCP-682 had seen sparing evidence throughout
the Backrooms of abandoned human civilizations,

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:58.310
but the ruins of Level 23 were closer in appearances
to the structures built by the people of 682’s

00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.310
native reality.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:05.370
They were similar to some of the great wonders
of the world - but with fundamental differences.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:09.520
For example, a number of near-replicas of
the Pyramids of Giza deviated in shape enough

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:13.070
from the originals to be arranged in a spherical
formation.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:17.520
The other buildings found within this area
of Level 23 had obvious counterparts, but

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.900
none of the architecture represented modern
design trends.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:24.800
The most advanced buildings were equivalent
to buildings in the frontrooms constructed

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.490
in and before 1000 A.D.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:32.490
In and among the ancient ruins could be found
a large variety of artifacts – all of which

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:36.979
seemed equally to be shoddy knock-offs of
relics from the frontrooms.

00:06:36.979 --> 00:06:41.830
SCP-682 stepped across the fragile pottery
and clay idols, quietly satisfied at the sight

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:47.349
of many telltale signs of civilizational collapse
and the utter lack of living humans.

00:06:47.349 --> 00:06:51.599
There were a few Clumps fiddling around in
the rubble, but 682 didn’t let them get

00:06:51.599 --> 00:06:54.400
away with existing in its presence.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:58.220
You dreadful rejects can return but not Jerry?

00:06:58.220 --> 00:06:59.720
How disgusting…

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:01.979
I miss Jerry.

00:07:01.979 --> 00:07:05.710
SCP-682 thoughts turned to its lost companion,
Entity 7.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:10.610
The blue hyacinth macaw had been the only
tolerable presence that 682 had known within

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:15.470
The Backrooms and sadly, in the hard-to-destroy
reptile’s entire existence.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:20.349
This hateful and terrific being had never
understood the meaning of love and compassion

00:07:20.349 --> 00:07:22.550
until Jerry had appeared to it.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:26.430
It was possible that they would never meet
again, and this somber realization weighed

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:29.280
heavily on 682’s mind.

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:33.710
The big lizard continued through the glow
room and noticed an unusual plaque scrawled

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:34.930
in rough latin.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:40.570
While 682 was not an avid reader, its adaptive
capabilities allowed it to translate the message

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:44.710
that was left behind by whatever beings previously
inhabited Level 23.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:46.039
It read:

00:07:46.039 --> 00:07:49.870
“We dedicate this Great Sphere of Giza to
the Great Gardener

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:53.349
In hopes of forgiveness for the great wrong
we have committed

00:07:53.349 --> 00:07:58.909
Already our purple eyes have turned green
We have started to return to the earth, forgotten

00:07:58.909 --> 00:08:02.800
and overgrown
Our only hope is that, alone and petrified,

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:07.490
we will not disappear
As Architects of a failed project.”

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:11.950
The first sentence was apparently a clear
reference to the spherical Great Pyramid that

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:16.840
682 had come across earlier, but the significance
of the rest remained a mystery.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:21.550
Whoever these failed architects were, there
was no trace of them left on this planetoid.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:25.870
SCP-682 didn’t mourn them of course, and
it felt almost content to know that whatever

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:31.060
grand project they had in store had crumbled,
leaving their ruins occupied by the likes

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:32.060
of clumps.

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:36.529
It served them right for existing, for attempting
to create something.

00:08:36.529 --> 00:08:40.810
Their sadness was proof enough that they’d
learned their lesson and had long since faded

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:42.300
into the ether.

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:46.380
Maybe that’s all the Backrooms was in the
end: a series of failed attempts at building

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:51.550
worlds that would ultimately be forgotten
when time and people moved on to bigger and

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:52.680
better projects.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:59.800
SCP-682 mused on these thoughts as it proceeded
down into the very core of Level 23.

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:03.750
To its surprise, a sight of remarkable beauty
awaited the reptile within.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:08.519
There, countless roots found and embraced
each other surrounding the gravity-locked

00:09:08.519 --> 00:09:14.520
orb of luminescent water - an apparent source
of light, nutrients, and, ultimately life

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:17.590
for the greenery of Level 23.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:23.270
This was the heart of the level, and it was
fittingly known as The Heart of Water.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:28.959
682 stared for a long time at the heart of
water, and it wasn’t really sure why.

00:09:28.959 --> 00:09:33.510
Naturally occurring wonders like this held
little appeal to the reptile, but somehow

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.160
this one was different.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:41.130
Perhaps it was because at this moment, SCP-682
truly realized how far it had come from its

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.640
containment cell at Site 19.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:48.190
It had endured every hardship the Backrooms
had thrown its way, and now it was looking

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:53.820
upon the Heart of Water - an object that could
never have fathomed existing and could never

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:59.930
have reached unless it became truly free and
uninhibited: no longer subject to the whims

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:01.160
of the Foundation.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:08.570
Then, the most unusual thing happened to SCP-682:
a function of its physiology that was so rarely

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:11.170
seen or utilized.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:14.660
SCP-682 shed a single tear.

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:18.840
It flowed down the reptilian creature’s
snout and then, arrested by the gravitational

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:24.310
pull of the heart of water, floated away and
vanished into the liquid mass.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:29.750
This was a private moment for 682 that not
even Jerry was here to see, and yet, the fall

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:34.410
of this tear may have solidified a change
in 682.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:38.029
It was a mixed feeling of independence and
detachment.

00:10:38.029 --> 00:10:43.410
For most of its journey through the Backrooms,
SCP-682 had felt an urge to completely clear

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:48.270
the abyss and show no mercy to every entity
that existed within it.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:53.060
Whether it manifested as determination or
spite, that urge had been the overriding feeling

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:58.399
that had driven SCP-682 to progress through
every level of the Backrooms in sequential

00:10:58.399 --> 00:10:59.399
order.

00:10:59.399 --> 00:11:03.410
But these new feelings made it realize that
even that would be playing into the hands

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:05.060
of the Backrooms.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:10.690
SCP-682 once thought that the Backrooms were
a cold and indifferent place, like an endless

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:15.530
universe that arbitrarily created and destroyed
all the beings that existed in it without

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.020
purpose or reason.

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:22.339
But that was not the case, and in fact, it
seemed more likely that the complete opposite

00:11:22.339 --> 00:11:23.590
was true.

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:28.750
The Backrooms was imbued by its unknown creators
with so much obvious intention that it was

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.310
practically a sentient being.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:37.180
The Backrooms was heavily invested in taking
itself seriously, in revering every detail

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:43.209
that made each level distinctive, and giving
every entity and hazards a specific method

00:11:43.209 --> 00:11:47.899
of ruining the experience of all wanderers
that passed through.

00:11:47.899 --> 00:11:53.380
SCP-682 could now see The Backrooms for what
it actually was – a desperate, pathetic

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:58.459
thing clawing for attention but forever doomed
to be obscure and unloved.

00:11:58.459 --> 00:12:04.810
It was even sadder than an indifferent universe,
because it was a constructed universe that

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:09.820
had no greater meaning than to be acknowledged
for simply being something where nothing once

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:10.870
was.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:15.600
It could even be said that the words on the
plaque of the glow room in Level 23 were the

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:21.209
ultimate admission of hopelessness and that
there was nothing waiting for SCP-682 or any

00:12:21.209 --> 00:12:27.030
other wanderer but the similar statements
of failed architects all the way down.

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:31.910
And that was to say nothing of all the once-ambitious
works within the Backrooms that had been erased

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:33.500
by happenstance.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:39.000
Who could even say that the numbers that corresponded
to Backrooms levels that SCP-682 had already

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.720
traversed were even the correct ones?

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:46.700
There could potentially be one or more entirely
different numerical sequences to the levels

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:50.230
that were equally as true to the ones who
labeled them as such.

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:56.070
If the Backrooms didn’t want to be known,
to be documented, to be expanded upon, I doubt

00:12:56.070 --> 00:13:00.650
that such rigid assignments of numbers would
have been acceptable by its creators.

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:07.010
It was in realizing all of this that 682 remembered
the elderly explorer that had flung him to

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.010
Level 23.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:12.649
While it was true that things hadn’t gone
the reptile’s way in that encounter, it

00:13:12.649 --> 00:13:17.019
was questionable who the real winner was when
it was clear that the man had dedicated the

00:13:17.019 --> 00:13:20.940
best years of his life to researching and
wandering the Backrooms.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:26.740
Sure, he had mastered some neat parlor tricks
with the magical items native to this reality,

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:31.190
but to be a Master of the Backrooms was no
better than SCP-682 declaring itself master

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:34.890
of the acid tank in its prior containment
cell.

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:39.810
That Elderly Man with the trinkets could keep
his hollow victory, because 682 would still

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:44.300
be alive and kicking when that human’s bones
were nothing more than setting dressing left

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:48.600
behind in some heretofore untouched level
of The Backrooms.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:53.449
His fate would be the same as the rest of
the Backrooms eventually: a joke with no real

00:13:53.449 --> 00:13:56.460
setup and punchline forgotten.

00:13:56.460 --> 00:14:01.460
To attempt to complete or destroy or uncover
the mysteries behind the Backrooms was exactly

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:06.810
what the loathsome cluster of disjointed concepts
wanted, and 682 was done with giving this

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:09.400
liminal nightmare the satisfaction.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:14.800
Sometimes the only way to win a game is not
to play the game at all, and that was precisely

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:19.620
how SCP-682 would approach the Backrooms from
here on out.

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:24.060
Maybe it would be trapped forever, or maybe
it would be sent home at any moment, but caring

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:28.120
about the outcome either way was a waste of
precious brainpower.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:33.990
There was only one way to deal with the desperate
neediness of the Backrooms, and that was embracing

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:39.459
and becoming internally the cold, indifferent
universe that it could never be.

00:14:39.459 --> 00:14:47.630
And that was now what SCP-682 would be: enlightened
and fully detached from this reality.

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:52.380
It strode out of the heart of water and into
another glow room, only to find an outpost

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:55.339
of Major Explorer’s Group waiting for it.

00:14:55.339 --> 00:14:57.970
Let’s try something new.

00:14:57.970 --> 00:15:03.730
SCP-682 easily broke down the door, and found
itself surrounded by panicked humans.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:07.889
Many of them were wielding pump-action squirt
guns and had begun spraying 682 with what

00:15:07.889 --> 00:15:10.080
seemed to be almond-flavored water.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:14.270
SCP-682 didn’t react to these attacks at
all, and slowly wandered towards the humans

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:16.149
with no particular urgency.

00:15:16.149 --> 00:15:21.990
“Pardon my intrusion,” SCP-682 said, grinning
with as much politeness as it could muster.

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:26.430
“Do any of you fine people know the way
back to Level 9?”

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:29.350
The humans shuddered, unsure how to answer.

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:34.579
They stood their silence until one brave soul
came forth and spoke to SCP-682.

00:15:34.579 --> 00:15:38.880
“There’s a gateway inside of this outpost
that can take you to the next level.”

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.259
Said the explorer.

00:15:40.259 --> 00:15:44.339
“But it appears to be one-way since whatever
was on the other side appears to no longer

00:15:44.339 --> 00:15:45.339
exist.”

00:15:45.339 --> 00:15:47.950
“What do you mean it no longer exists?”

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:53.470
SCP-682 asked, trying against its better judgment
to make sense of the circumstances.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.710
The explorer nodded and went on, seemingly
motivated by fear:

00:15:56.710 --> 00:16:01.529
“We mean it’s no longer part of any current
archive of Backrooms-related phenomena, and

00:16:01.529 --> 00:16:05.100
even its name will likely be erased soon,
not that having the name would provide any

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:06.120
consolation.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:09.620
After all, there’s still no telling what
is on the other side, and if it was ever what

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:12.050
the explorers who reported on it claimed it
was.”

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:14.600
Now, this was an unsettling development.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:20.430
682 had only just started to come to terms
with the instability of reality in the Backrooms,

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:24.769
and the notion that a level could be totally
wiped from existence and leave behind a gateway

00:16:24.769 --> 00:16:29.139
to absolutely nowhere was chilling even to
the immortal lizard.

00:16:29.139 --> 00:16:33.680
What would happen to 682 if the reptile stepped
through this gateway?

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:37.949
Would it find itself in the place that the
gateway was once and still is connected to

00:16:37.949 --> 00:16:42.910
or would it simply disappear into the void
as if it were never there at all?

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:47.759
Because this was the Backrooms there was always
a third option too, as well as countless others

00:16:47.759 --> 00:16:49.730
that defied all logic.

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:56.160
So now the question facing SCP-682 was – to
step into the unknown or to remain here in

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.709
Level 23 with the Major Explorer’s Group.

00:16:58.709 --> 00:17:01.791
It was a difficult decision, to say the least.

00:17:01.791 --> 00:17:05.699
The humans looked on as SCP-682 carefully
weighed its options.

00:17:05.699 --> 00:17:09.429
Eventually, the reptile opened its mouth to
speak on the matter.

00:17:09.429 --> 00:17:12.339
“I’ll give it some thought.”

00:17:12.339 --> 00:17:13.339
SCP-682 said.

00:17:13.339 --> 00:17:18.339
“You’ve been very helpful for a disgusting
human, so for the time being, I will permit

00:17:18.339 --> 00:17:21.189
you to continue your meaningless existence.

00:17:21.189 --> 00:17:23.880
And I guess that includes the rest of your
outpost.”

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:27.030
“Oh, that’s… well, thank you…

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:28.030
I…

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:29.030
thank you.”

00:17:29.030 --> 00:17:31.320
The human stammered.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:35.030
SCP-682 turned and began to walk back towards
The Heart of Water.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:39.600
It intended to take its time with its choice,
since progress through the levels of the Backrooms

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:43.830
was no longer something that the reptile would
be pursuing with reckless abandon.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:48.690
It heavily considered going back on its words
and slaughtering all the members of the major

00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:53.350
explorer’s group in this outpost - as it
had done in all the other outposts.

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:58.090
But it was plain to see that a human trapped
in the Backrooms barely qualified as living,

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:02.620
because nothing could be worse than being
permanently stuck in the torturous abyss.

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:07.550
682 had no idea whether pure spite towards
them was what made sparing their lives so

00:18:07.550 --> 00:18:12.890
compelling or something else had motivated
that decision, but regardless - the hard-to-destroy

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:16.830
reptile did not destroy the humans of level
23.

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:21.360
As it exited the base, the brave human that
had spoken to it called out:

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:22.360
“Wait, lizard!

00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:25.039
I have to know: what are you?”

00:18:25.039 --> 00:18:27.289
682 stopped and stared at the human.

00:18:27.289 --> 00:18:29.770
“It’s just… we need to catalog you.

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:32.530
I’ve never seen anything else in the Backrooms
like you.”

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:34.200
682 breathed out.

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:37.100
It sounded almost like a surrender.

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:41.409
“I am Entity 682.”

00:18:41.409 --> 00:18:46.360
After those words left its jaws, 682 wandered
away from the human until it was once again

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:47.820
sitting by The Heart of Water.

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:51.160
It didn’t think about the choice or the
gateway immediately.

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:56.190
For now, Entity 682 was peacefully reminiscing
back to the quality time it had spent with

00:18:56.190 --> 00:19:01.950
Entity 7 Jerry in this pointless and nonsensical
place known as the Backrooms.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.340
They would meet again.

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:06.660
That was the one thing 682 could be sure of.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:10.080
Somehow, someway, they would meet again.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:15.341
An indeterminate amount of time later, over
24 levels away from the reptile in the Frontrooms

00:19:15.341 --> 00:19:20.330
– the reality which it had no-clipped out
of so many days and weeks ago, the researchers

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:25.950
of the SCP Foundation had gathered together
and were celebrating an unforeseen event.

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:29.750
Almost all of them had long since given up
hope that it could ever happen.

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:35.350
And yet, here they were, standing before the
05 Council and all the illustrious scientists

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:38.659
and soldiers that had worked to make this
day a reality.

00:19:38.659 --> 00:19:43.280
Everyone watched in total amazement as the
heads of the Foundation declared the keter-class

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:49.410
SCP-682 “hard to destroy reptile” permanently
neutralized.

